What is objectID and timestamp from an object?

An ObjectId is a unique identifier automatically created by MongoDB for each document in the _id field.
An ObjectId is a 12-byte value containing:
---Timestamp → creation time of document
---Machine identifier
---Process ID
---Random/increment value

